    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d137-a1">

                <pb facs="0145" n="133" xml:id="pg133"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Annex]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Appendix to SWNCC
                        256, January 30</hi><anchor n="74" xml:id="d137-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Message to</hi>
                    SCAP</p>
                <p>Subject is convocation of Allied Council for Japan. U.S. Government considers
                    that it would be impracticable to organize Allied Council until Far Eastern
                    Commission is functioning in Washington. Following is for your guidance: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>The State Department will obtain from the governments concerned and
                            will furnish to you the names of other representatives on the Allied
                            Council for Japan.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>When the Far Eastern Commission is functioning in Washington, you will
                            be informed so that you, as chairman, may convene the first meeting of
                            the Allied Council for Japan.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>If the representatives designated by Russian, Chinese and British
                            Commonwealth governments are in Tokyo, you should invite them by direct
                            communication to participate in first meeting. If they have not yet
                            arrived in Tokyo, your invitation should be forwarded to JCS in order that State Department may
                            forward it to governments concerned.</item>
                    </list></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
